            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Polyurethane will not bond reliably to cured silicone — almost nothing does. Silicone over cured polyurethane is more forgiving but still not recommended without checking the manufacturer's guidance. In practice, remove the old bead entirely and clean the joint back to bare material.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Which should I use around windows?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "If the joint will be painted as part of the trim, polyurethane or a paintable hybrid. If it is a bead against glass or an unpainted frame, silicone. Many exterior window jobs use both — polyurethane where the frame meets the wall and gets painted, silicone where the glazing meets the frame.",
